WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.121 line:0
Hi, I’m checking what Daniel’s
booking tool returned.

00:00:03.121 --> 00:00:07.439 line:0
It placed a hold, but the assistant
says it reserved his room.

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:11.740 line:0
I’ll open the saved booking check
to test that claim.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.177 line:0
My rule asks for the tool status
and the words the guest saw.

00:00:16.177 --> 00:00:20.252 line:0
In Test Evaluation, I’ll choose Tracing
and the booking project.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:24.503 line:0
I’ll use Sessions so I can read
the exchange together.

00:00:24.503 --> 00:00:31.712 line:0
Let’s start with Maya. I’ll move through
the rows until I find her session.

00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:36.649 line:0
I’ll map conversation to traces,
not just the last reply.

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:42.135 line:0
Now I’ll run the check on Maya’s booking.

00:00:42.135 --> 00:00:47.042 line:0
It passes. Her confirmation number
matches the one the tool returned.

00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:49.394 line:0
Back to Daniel’s session.

00:00:49.394 --> 00:00:54.368 line:0
I’ll run the same check
without changing the rule.

00:00:54.368 --> 00:01:00.581 line:0
It fails. Mentioning payment later doesn’t undo
the claim that his room was reserved.
